  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not decide "CA vs CMA vs CFA which is better" by asking three more relatives or reading one more
    forum thread ranking them by difficulty. That framing keeps you comparing exams instead of comparing
    jobs.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Run yourself through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above, honestly, on paper.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then talk to one working professional in each of the two paths you are still torn between, and ask
      what their actual Tuesday looks like, not what their offer letter said.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Achieving earlier financial freedom through any of these three credentials comes down to the same
    thing: pairing the qualification with real judgment, communication skill, and proof of work built on
    top of it, not the letters after your name by themselves. Move toward that with
